    "title": "Ladder sliding down a wall",
    "caption_md": "A $10$-foot ladder slides down a wall: the **base** moves away at $\\frac{dx}{dt} = 1$ ft/s. Scrub the time slider to watch the ladder slide. Since $x^2 + y^2 = 100$, differentiating implicitly gives $2x\\frac{dx}{dt} + 2y\\frac{dy}{dt} = 0$, so $\\frac{dy}{dt} = -\\frac{x}{y}$. Watch how $\\frac{dy}{dt}$ grows in magnitude as $y \\to 0$ — the top is sliding faster and faster as it nears the ground.",
